What:           /dev/nq-nci
Date:           November 2026
Contact:        linux-nfc@lists.infradead.org
Description:
                Raw NCI I2C transport for the cannong vendor NFC HAL.
                Reads and writes transfer up to 512 bytes. Probe requires a
                complete CORE_RESET_RSP with success status. This verifies
                transport, not HAL initialization, firmware or tag operation.

                PN544_SET_PWR (_IOW(0xe9, 1, unsigned int)) takes a scalar:
                  0: power off
                  1: power on in normal mode
                  2: firmware-download mode with VEN reset
                  4: assert firmware-download pin
                  5: VEN reset pulse
                  6: deassert firmware-download pin
                Modes 2, 4 and 6 require the firmware-download GPIO.
                Mode 3 (eSE ISO reset) returns EOPNOTSUPP. Invalid power
                arguments return EINVAL.

                The following legacy operations return EOPNOTSUPP because
                their eSE/arbitration semantics are not implemented:
                  P61_SET_SPI_PWR, P61_GET_PWR_STATUS, P61_SET_WIRED_ACCESS,
                  P544_SET_NFC_SERVICE_PID, P544_GET_ESE_ACCESS,
                  P544_SET_POWER_SCHEME, P544_REL_SVDD_WAIT,
                  PN544_SET_DWNLD_STATUS (JCOP download state),
                  P544_REL_DWPONOFF_WAIT, P544_SECURE_TIMER_SESSION,
                  NFCC_INITIAL_CORE_RESET_NTF.
                Unknown ioctls return ENOTTY. There is no eSE/payment or
                screen-off NFC wake capability implied by this endpoint.
